# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Thunderstorm Simulator — .gitignore
# Policy (see CLAUDE.md, scenarios/README.md): raw netCDF is regenerable and NEVER
# committed. Scenario packages are multi-GB and live in scenarios/ INSIDE the project
# folder, but their payload stays out of git HISTORY (resolved 2026-07-20 — no LFS
# anywhere in this repo). manifest.json is the exception and IS tracked: it is the
# versioned contract UE checks. Nothing >10 MB in plain git.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Simulation raw output (regenerable, disposable by design) ────────────────
*.nc
*.nc4
*.netcdf
*.dat
*.grads
*.ctl
sim/**/output/
sim/**/*.rst
**/restart/
**/rst/

# ── VDB volumes & scenario packages (multi-GB payload; in-tree, out of history) ──
*.vdb
# Dense-array fixtures the VDB writer consumes (regenerable; can be large):
*.densevol
pipeline/vdbwriter/synthetic_seq/
scenarios/**/*.vdb
scenarios/**/*.exr
scenarios/**/*.png
scenarios/**/*.jpg
scenarios/**/frames/
# Web-viewer bricks (diorama/): gzipped quantized volumes, regenerable.
# NOTE the trailing /* rather than /: git does NOT descend into an excluded
# DIRECTORY, so `scenarios/**/web/` would make the negation below unreachable and
# web_manifest.json could never be tracked. Excluding the directory's CONTENTS
# instead keeps it re-includable. (web/ is flat -- no subdirectories to miss.)
scenarios/**/web/*
# Keep scenario manifests/contracts and small docs tracked:
!scenarios/**/manifest.json
# web_manifest.json is the web package's contract, and for a WEB-ONLY package
# (owner decision 2026-07-22, Phase 3 T2) it is the ONLY contract there is: the
# diorama is the sole consumer this phase, it already checks web_format_version's
# major, and no top-level manifest.json is written because manifest.build() is
# SVT-shaped (per-VDB frame records, SVT_TEXTURE_MAP, ue_placement_rule) and no
# VDB ships. Tracking it is what keeps "the contract is version-controlled" true
# for supercell_333m. ~45-150 KB each; the multi-GB bricks stay ignored.
!scenarios/**/web/web_manifest.json
!scenarios/**/*.md

# ── Diorama web viewer (diorama/) ────────────────────────────────────────────
diorama/node_modules/
diorama/dist/

# ── Python (pipeline/) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.Python
.venv/
venv/
env/
.env
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.conda/

# ── Unreal Engine (unreal/) — standard UE ignores ────────────────────────────
unreal/**/Binaries/
unreal/**/Intermediate/
unreal/**/Saved/
unreal/**/DerivedDataCache/
unreal/**/Build/
unreal/**/.vs/
unreal/**/*.VC.db
unreal/**/*.opensdf
unreal/**/*.sdf
unreal/**/*.suo
unreal/**/*.sln
# UE binary assets are large; if versioned later, do it via Git LFS (decide first).
unreal/**/*.uasset
unreal/**/*.umap

# ── Editors / OS cruft ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ── Temp / scratch (kept out of the repo tree by policy) ─────────────────────
tmp/
temp/
scratch/
*.log
